so: Wrela Stdlib Surface (Runnable)
so:
so: This file captures the **public stdlib surface contract** as implemented
so: in `core/compiler/stdlib/`. It is intentionally lightweight: it
so: checks that critical surface helpers exist and behave at a minimal level.
so:
so: The language spec (`core/spec/spec.wr`) does not define stdlib semantics.
so: Stdlib surface can evolve faster than core language rules.

use:
    from_string,
    to_string,
    length
from bytes

use:
    new,
    get,
    set
from map

use push from list

use:
    int,
    float
from parse


so: ------------------------------------------------------------
so: 1) Bytes helpers


to test_bytes_helpers() -> Nothing:
    bytes = from_string("hi")
    assert value length(bytes) == 2
    assert value to_string(bytes) == "hi"


so: ------------------------------------------------------------
so: 2) Map helpers


to test_map_new_and_accessors() -> Nothing:
    m = new()
    set(m, "k", 7)
    assert value get(m, "k") == 7


so: ------------------------------------------------------------
so: 3) List helpers


to test_list_push_builtin() -> Nothing:
    items = [1, 2]
    push(items, 3)
    assert value items == [1, 2, 3]


so: ------------------------------------------------------------
so: 4) Parse helpers


to test_parse_int_and_float() -> Nothing:
    assert value (int("12") otherwise 0) == 12
    assert value (float("1.5") otherwise 0.0) == 1.5


so: ------------------------------------------------------------
so: 5) Stdlib types and classes
so:
so: The following types/classes are part of the public stdlib surface.
so: This spec does not attempt to exhaustively test them.
so:
so: - Env: get, get_or, get_as_bool, get_as_int, set, load
so: - Auth: configure, create_user, verify_password, issue_jwt, verify_jwt,
so:         issue_email_token, verify_email_token, oauth_login
so: - RBAC: create_role, assign_role, check, permissions_for
so: - Files: upload_stream, signed_url, metadata, delete, set_acl
so: - Jobs: configure, enqueue, process, dead_letter
so: - Schedule: cron, every, at
so: - Search: index, remove, query
so: - Realtime: configure, on_connect, join, leave, broadcast, send
so: - PubSub: configure
so: - Log / Logger (logging helpers + configure)
so: - Runtime (runtime configuration)
so: - RateLimit: check, ip
so: - Admin: enable
so: - StorageConfig + StorageClient (storage_* helpers)
so: - storage_open function
so: - HttpRequest + HttpResponse helpers
so: - HttpServer helpers
